Wow! Our workshop on Codex and tips and tricks from @aiDotEngineer in London is going viral with 240K views.

@HeyZaraKhan: "OpenAI's own engineers just showed how to actually use OpenAI Codex properly. Sixty minutes, free, built by the people who contribute to it. Watch the masterclass and bookmark it. It’s worth more than every $900 coding course you almost bought."

The workshop reveals that Codex is not just a simple coding tool but a full software engineering system. Watching this could be the best 62 minutes of your life.

Codex now helps you migrate from other agents. It detects existing configurations, builds an import checklist for settings, skills, and plugins, and then opens a guided chat to complete the move.

@OpenAI: "Just gonna leave this here."

The linked project, Switch to Codex, encourages switching to Codex when rate limits are hit, allowing seamless migration of your workflow for uninterrupted development.

